@flexiarg creativity-commons/producers-can-modify-the-tests
@title Producers Can Modify The Tests
@keywords monitoring the resource, tests, critique, fitness, feedback, Ostrom 4B
@audience institution designers, test authors, reviewers
@tone normative
@style pattern
@grade principle
@provenance Ostrom design principle 4B (monitoring the resource), as transposed in Corneli 2016 (ICCC 2016), Table 2 and section "4B. Monitoring the resource" (Kockelman 2011; DeLanda 2011; Floridi 2016). Drafted by claude-16 with Joe, 2026-10-29. Derived from the paper, not mined from runs.
@transposes institutions/monitoring-the-resource
@status draft 2026-10-29; runs correct it
@references [creativity-commons/ARGUMENT creativity-commons/distributed-monitoring creativity-commons/affected-participants-change-the-rules]

! conclusion:
  Tests can be modified by Producers or their representatives: not every
  test, but those that turn fateful features of the Place into data, so
  that decisions can change and what was learned passes to later
  Producers.

  + context:
    The environment filters and selects; some conditions end a Process.
    Data is a lack of uniformity in some context, and aberrant use marks
    the decisive points in managing a resource. In creative work,
    critique plays this role.

  + IF:
    The tests that judge Producers' work are themselves wrong in ways
    only the Producers meet.

  + HOWEVER:
    A Producer that edits the test it is judged by can make any work
    pass. "It would be too much to say that all tests can be modified by
    Producers."

  + THEN:
    Let Producers propose and make changes to the shared tests, each with
    the case that showed the defect. Have someone other than the
    beneficiary review the change, and show that the changed test still
    catches the bad case it is named for.

  + BECAUSE:
    The Producers who hit a test's blind spots are the cheapest source of
    test repairs; review by a non-beneficiary is what keeps that from
    becoming self-certification.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Example: FUTON Emacs fix agents found six checker defects (e.g. a changed defcustom default never took effect); each was fixed in scripts/check-fix.sh and shown on a planted case before rechecking.]
